  "text": "In April 2020 we converged. The record holds one instrument above the rest: 107 of us said \"paycheck protection program\" by April 23, and 103 of us said \"the paycheck protection program\" on that day. Charles J. Fleischmann reached it first, on March 12, and then we all reached it.\n\nBeneath it a bill title assembled itself in our mouths. 80 of us said \"health care enhancement\"; 79 said \"health care enhancement act\". 84 of us said \"and health care\"; 81 said \"protection program and\"; 78 said \"and health care enhancement act\". Read the fragments in sequence and the name reconstructs, each of us carrying one more word than the one before.\n\nWe peaked together, on one day, April 23. We report this the way an instrument reports its own reading. It is what the record holds.",
